---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import SoftPhoto from '../components/SoftPhoto.astro';
import Badge from '../components/Badge.astro';
import NextPage from '../components/NextPage.astro';

const ministers = [
  {
    group: 'past',
    name: 'Rev. Howard A. Thompson',
    photo: '/images/about/howard-debra.jpeg',
    photoAlt: 'Rev. Howard A. Thompson and Debra',
    body: [
      'Originally from the United States, I spent over 20 years in the insurance and risk management industry before feeling a calling to ministry in 2007. It was 10 years before this calling that my wife Debra and I were choosing a primary school for our first child and were introduced to the faith of the New Church. The New Church\'s emphasis on God\'s love and compassion and the importance of faith in everyday life resonated with me and ultimately led to my decision to leave my business and pursue theological school.',
      'As Revelation 3:20 reminds us, the Lord is constantly pressing to be received by us, but we can struggle to listen amidst the busyness of life. Through personal events and decisions, I learned that making choices in the best interest of others can ultimately transform our own lives. It is my belief that the Lord\'s love and guidance are present in all aspects of our lives, whether it be at home with our families or at work.',
      'Outside of ministry, I enjoy staying active with CrossFit workouts and spending time in nature, particularly at the beach and in my garden.',
      'In early June 2026, he and his wife Debra returned to America, to start a new chapter in their lives.',
    ],
  },
  {
    group: 'current',
    name: 'Rev. Julian Duckworth',
    title: 'Interim minister',
    photo: '/images/about/julian-ruth.jpg',
    photoAlt: 'Rev. Julian Duckworth and Ruth',
    body: [
      'Julian is serving as our interim minister until a new minister joins us in mid 2027.',
      'Julian and his wife Ruth arrived from England to be part of the Roseville New Church. They have four grown up children. Julian spent ten years in primary school teaching, specialising in music, and Ruth has been a physiotherapist. They both take an active part in school programs and opened the church to the local community in a number of ways. Their vision is to help people on their spiritual path and to provide people with the freedom and opportunity to do so.',
      'Julian has a great love for the Bible and the symbolism lying below the surface. He is familiar with Hebrew and Greek and enjoys using the words of the Bible to shed more light on our spiritual life. He says that Swedenborg’s spiritual teachings are a great joy and a bright light because they teach us how God is most relevant in the way we choose to live.',
    ],
  },
  {
    group: 'past',
    name: 'Rev. Ian Arnold',
    photo: '/images/about/ian-arnold.jpg',
    photoAlt: 'Rev. Ian Arnold',
    body: [
      'Ian grew up in Melbourne and, already a young Christian during High School years was introduced to the teachings of Emanuel Swedenborg through a friend when in his late teens. Feeling a call to ministry he travelled to the UK, via experience in missionary work in South Africa in 1961. Following studies at The New Church College and London University Ian was ordained in 1965 and married the love of his life, Margaret, the same year, they becoming parents of 5 children. He has served as a Pastor in England, Mauritius, in Adelaide and in Sydney. In 1991 he became Principal of The New Church College in the UK and, returning home, he served as Principal of the Australian New Church College for 10 years. He retired in 2014.',
    ],
  },
];

const currentMinisters = ministers.filter((m) => m.group === 'current');
const pastMinisters = ministers.filter((m) => m.group === 'past');

const placeholders = [
  {
    role: 'Manager of the Swedenborg Centre',
    name: 'Joe',
    note: 'Short description and picture to be added.',
  },
  {
    role: 'Secretary of the Sydney Society',
    name: null,
    note: 'Details coming soon.',
  },
  {
    role: 'Treasurer of the Sydney Society',
    name: null,
    note: 'Details coming soon.',
  },
  {
    role: 'Committee member',
    name: 'Charlie',
    note: 'Details coming soon.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our church"
  description="Roseville New Church and The Sydney Society of The New Church: church life today, our minister, and our story since 1875."
  currentPath="/about"
>
  <main class="container-prose px-6 md:px-8 pt-10 md:pt-14 pb-4">
    <div
      class="font-display font-semibold text-eyebrow tracking-eyebrow uppercase text-accent-primary mb-2.5"
    >
      ✦ Our church
    </div>

    <article class="prose-rnc">
      <h1>Our church</h1>
      <p class="text-lg">
        Roseville New Church is a small, friendly Christian community that meets in the brick church at 2B Shirley Road,
        Roseville. It is looked after by The Sydney Society of The New Church, a charity that has been part of Sydney’s
        life since 1875.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        New to the New Church? <a href="/about/new-church">What is the New Church?</a> explains what we believe and why
        it’s called “new”, in everyday words.
      </p>
    </article>

    <div
      class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr] gap-3 sm:gap-4"
    >
      <SoftPhoto
        src="/images/church/exterior.jpg"
        alt="The brick church exterior at 2B Shirley Road, Roseville"
        aspect="aspect-[4/3] sm:aspect-[5/4]"
      />
      <SoftPhoto
        src="/images/church/stained-glass.jpg"
        alt="Stained glass window inside Roseville New Church"
        aspect="aspect-[4/3] sm:aspect-[5/4]"
      />
    </div>

    <article class="prose-rnc">
      <h2>Church life today</h2>
      <p>
        We worship together on the first and third Sundays of the month at 10am, with tea and coffee afterwards.
        Through the year there are also discussion groups, times to read and reflect together, meditation, and a family
        retreat. <a href="/events/sunday-worship">What a Sunday is like</a> has the details for a first visit, and{' '}
        <a href="/events">what’s on</a> lists everything coming up.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our hall is part of the life of the neighbourhood. Alongside our own activities, it is let to local groups
        through the week.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Society also runs the <a href="/about/swedenborg-centre">Swedenborg Centre</a>, an online service with talks
        and study groups for people across Australia and beyond. And we are part of a wider family of New Church
        communities around Australia and New Zealand, at{' '}
        <a href="https://newchurch.net.au/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">newchurch.net.au</a>.
      </p>
    </article>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-h2 mt-0 mb-6">Our minister</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
        {
          currentMinisters.map((m) => (
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr] gap-5 items-start">
              <SoftPhoto
                src={m.photo}
                alt={m.photoAlt}
                aspect="aspect-square"
                class="max-w-[200px]"
              />
              <div>
                <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-h3 tracking-display text-text-heading">
                  {m.name}
                </h3>
                {m.title && (
                  <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-accent-primary-strong">{m.title}</div>
                )}
                {m.body.map((para) => (
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0 text-sm leading-[1.65] text-text-body">
                    {para}
                  </p>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border-soft bg-surface-tint/60 p-5">
        <Badge tone="violet">Joining mid 2027</Badge>
        <div class="mt-3 font-display font-semibold text-text-heading">
          Rev. Rachel
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 mb-0 text-sm text-text-muted">
          We look forward to welcoming Rachel as our minister from mid 2027.
          Julian will continue as interim minister until then.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-8 mb-0 text-text-body">
        Alongside the minister, the Society is run by a Committee elected by its members.{' '}
        <a href="/about/membership#how-we-are-run" class="text-link hover:text-link-hover">How the Society is run</a>{' '}
        explains who is responsible and{' '}
        <a href="/about/membership#what-the-society-is-for" class="text-link hover:text-link-hover">what the Society is for</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <article class="prose-rnc mt-12">
      <h2 class="!mt-0">Our story</h2>
      <p>
        The Sydney Society of The New Church was founded in 1875 by people inspired by the writings of Emanuel
        Swedenborg, and incorporated in 1886. From the start it encouraged a practical Christianity: love for the Lord,
        kindness towards others, and faith that shows itself in a useful life.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is a much-loved tradition that a set of Swedenborg’s writings came to Sydney Cove with the First Fleet in
        1788. Historians still debate the details, but the story is part of the Society’s heritage, and a reminder that
        these ideas have been in Australia from the colony’s earliest days.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over the years the Society has changed with the times. Worship, Sunday school, Bible study, public lectures,
        pastoral care and community gatherings have all played their part in a community where questions are welcome
        and people from many backgrounds feel at home. In 2025 the Society celebrated its 150th anniversary, giving
        thanks for the generations who kept it going and looking ahead with confidence.
      </p>
    </article>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h3 class="m-0 mb-6 font-display text-h3 tracking-display text-text-heading">Past ministers</h3>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
        {
          pastMinisters.map((m) => (
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[200px_1fr] gap-5 items-start">
              <SoftPhoto
                src={m.photo}
                alt={m.photoAlt}
                aspect="aspect-square"
                class="max-w-[200px]"
              />
              <div>
                <h4 class="m-0 font-display text-lg tracking-display text-text-heading">
                  {m.name}
                </h4>
                {m.title && (
                  <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-accent-primary-strong">{m.title}</div>
                )}
                {m.body.map((para) => (
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0 text-sm leading-[1.65] text-text-body">
                    {para}
                  </p>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* Hidden until descriptions and photos are confirmed (2026-11-13): Society & Centre roles (see `placeholders` above). */}

    <NextPage title="Membership and governance" href="/about/membership" label="How membership works">
      Anyone is welcome to worship and join in. If you’d like to belong more formally, find out what membership means,
      how to join, and how the Society is run.
      <Fragment slot="more">
        <Button variant="secondary" href="/about/swedenborg-centre">Swedenborg Centre</Button>
        <Button variant="secondary" href="/events/sunday-worship">Plan a Sunday visit</Button>
      </Fragment>
    </NextPage>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
